**Bracket:** beats Matt-Smith (B anchor) — Matt-Smith sources its thesis quote as "he told the press while promoting *House of the Dragon*"; this sources its equivalent to a named host, show, and month. Loses to Peter Thiel (A anchor) — Thiel's Tolkien thread runs childhood-to-adult; this draft has no childhood at all.

### Key observations

**What's genuinely strong.** The Mixtral magnet-link release — 87GB torrent posted to X, no blog post for three days — is a real signature detail, and the piece earns it: *"He did not describe non-revocability that week. He shipped it."* The said-vs-spent ledger table is a bespoke form that includes the row that damages its own thesis. And the critic section states the limit of its own claim rather than absorbing the counterevidence: *"Type 6 explains his response to the fallout. It has nothing to say about the decision."*

**Three findings the automated checks missed:**

1. **The contrast-pair engine survived the regex, not the reader.** Lint and quality-report both return 0, and the draft's own ledger cites that as proof the contradiction is "carried by scene, chronology and causality." But the move is there six times in unregexed forms — including *"Read as marketing it is a stunt; read as architecture it is the whole argument in one gesture,"* which is literally *looked like X, was really Y* in semicolon form. Cap threshold is two. Writing capped at 8.

2. **The TESTIMONY LEDGER is stale, overstating by two.** It claims 7 qualifying quotes; 5 survive in the body. The Elad Gil quote was cut in the second pass (the fingerprint ledger on line 127 records the cut — the two ledgers contradict each other), and the Moyroud/FT quote never appears at all.

3. **The source audit's clean bill covers less than it looks.** It reported "no quoted material in slot" for *both* the empathy turn and the close, so its 7-inline/0-untagged result never touched the sections where three unsourced subject quotes sit — including "The safest technologies today are the open source technologies," which is the load-bearing quote of the empathy-turn section.

Also capped: the phobic/counterphobic mechanics paragraph does its resolving work in the body, outside both the diagnosis section and a Rabbit Hole that already has a wing section waiting for it. Enneagram 8.

Body is 3,899 words against a 3,200–3,900 band — one word under the top. Not padded, but worth watching.

**The ceiling is research, not editing.** Items 1–5 in the sidecar's TO REACH A are all revision-pass work worth roughly a point across Evidence/Writing/Enneagram. But the piece begins at a 2018 doctorate — the working notes cut the middle-school coding detail as farm-sourced and omitted the parents on source conflict. Reaching A needs new sourcing on what formed him before the institutions did.

